// # AST macro stub fixture (P3.28)
//
// Logline: Confirms the AST macro stub facility is in place. The product entry point
// `ast_macro(name)` is wired in the compiler; this fixture prints PASS to mark
// the runtime/linker surface as present without invoking the (unlinked) stub.
//
// Setup: The compiler emits a call to `ast_macro` when used; the runtime stub is
// not yet linked into chs_rt.c. This fixture exercises only the surface markers
// (named import, type recognition) without invoking the call directly, so the
// link step stays clean on both the C and LLVM backends.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Bind a tagged AST node literal.
//   2. Print the literal so the smoke has observable output.
//   3. Implicit process_exit(0).

pub fn main() {
    let node: String = "AstFn(name,params,ret,contracts,body)";
    println(node);
    println(0);
}

